@startuml
title 3.5.5 Train a custom matching model
caption UC-104 | Planned | Proposed design
skinparam monochrome true
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 0
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam LegendBackgroundColor white
skinparam style strictuml
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
show footbox
<style>
lifeLine {
    LineStyle 0
}
</style>
skinparam sequence {
    ParticipantBackgroundColor white
    ActorBackgroundColor white
    LifeLineBackgroundColor white
    LifeLineBorderColor black
    GroupBackgroundColor white
    GroupHeaderBackgroundColor white
}

' Source: docs/requirements/uc.md
' Main entity migration: Proposed entity; no migration
' One-table abstraction: related repository reads/writes stay inside the service.
actor "Admin" as Actor
participant "Proposed Training Console" as Page
participant "Proposed Matching API" as API
participant "Proposed Training Service" as Service
participant "matching_model_jobs" as Table <<proposed entity>>

Actor -> Page: 1: Open Train a custom matching model
activate Page
Page -> API: 2: Start training with approved dataset (proposed interface)
activate API
API -> API: 3: Validate access session, role and input
alt Valid request
API -> Service: 4: Train a custom matching model
activate Service
Service -> Service: 5: Require Admin; verify approved versioned and sanitized dataset
Service -> Table: 6: Proposed: create bounded reproducible training job
activate Table
Table --> Service: 7: Training job reference
deactivate Table
Service -> Service: 8: Queue controlled compute task; record parameters and provenance
Service -> Service: 9: Train candidate artifact; do not activate directly
Service --> API: 10: Training job
API --> Page: 11: HTTP 200: Training job
Page --> Actor: 12: Show authorized result
deactivate Service
else Invalid input, missing session or insufficient role
API --> Page: 4.1: Proposed rejection: invalid input / authorization
Page --> Actor: 4.2: Show appropriate error; retain form/draft
end
deactivate API
deactivate Page

legend left
Scope: No custom-model trainer, deployment workflow or migration exists for this proposed entity.
endlegend
@enduml
